<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Memory of the World Programme</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1992–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Memory of the World Register</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Memory of the World Programme is an initiative launched by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> in 1992 to protect the world's documentary heritage and make it accessible. Its international register lists <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>, archives, books, films and recordings judged to be of world significance, such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/annals-of-the-joseon-dynasty">Annals of the Joseon Dynasty</a> and the surviving volumes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bibliotheca-corviniana">Bibliotheca Corviniana</a>. Regional and national registers support the same aim.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/memory-of-the-world-programme.jpg" alt="Memory of the World Programme" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UNESCO · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Unesco_Memory_of_the_World_Logo_(English).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
